# PRD source of truth

The original Project 3 PRD is the sole source of truth for project scope, requirements, and completion.

Treat all self-created roadmaps, R/P checkpoints, progress trackers, and internal acceptance gates as historical references, not authorities.

Evaluate remaining work directly against the original PRD. Do not introduce new requirements, checkpoints, or approval processes unless explicitly requested.

Preserve existing security and spending safeguards, but do not mistake internal procedures for PRD requirements.

If the original PRD is unavailable, ask for it rather than substituting a traceability matrix or roadmap.

```text
# ❌ BAD
Treat Docs/ROADMAP.md or an R/P checkpoint as a requirement the PRD does not state.

# ✅ GOOD
Check the original Project 3 PRD. If it is missing, ask for it. Keep existing security and spend safeguards; do not add new gates.
```
